    "title": "Final score: No. 1 Duke, No. 5 St. John square off in Sweet 16 of men’s 2026 NCAA Tournament",
    "text": "Duke guard Caleb Foster (1) drives as St. John’s forward Dillon Mitchell defends during the second half in the Sweet 16 of the NCAA college basketball tournament, Friday, March 27, 2026, in Washington. (AP Photo/Stephanie Scarbrough) by: Hannah Leyva Posted: Mar 27, 2026 / 07:10 PM EDT Updated: Mar 27, 2026 / 09:31 PM EDT WASHINGTON (WNCN) — The last time Duke men’s basketball was in the nation’s capital, they defeated the then-No. 1 Michigan and took over their position. This time, the Blue Devils are the top seed in the NCAA Tournament and are looking to move on to the Elite 8. No. 1 Duke (34-2) will face off against No. 5 St. John’s (30-6) Friday night at Capital One Arena in the Sweet 16. Tip off is scheduled for 7:10 p.m. The Blue Devils defeated TCU 81-58 in a second round game in Greenville, S.C. last Saturday. Atlantic Coast Conference Player of the Year Cameron Boozer had a game-high 19 points and 11 rebounds, notching yet another double-double. Isaiah Evans chipped in 17 points and Dame Sarr added 14 points and eight boards. The Red Storm narrowly edged out Kansas on Saturday, wining 67-65 on a last-second layup by Dylan Darling — his only two points of the game. Zuby Ejiofor and Bryce Hopkins both scored 18 points for St. John’s, with the former adding nine rebounds and the latter grabbing seven boards. The winner moves on to the Elite 8 to face the winner of the other East regional matchup between No. 2 UConn and No. 3 Michigan State. Duke Blue Devils vs St. John’s Red Storm This event has ended. Find the latest Duke men’s basketball live scoreboard here.",
